  "narrative": "All new estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support and negative signed values oppose the claimed association. The PTEN-loss/STAT3-dependency association remains the most robust newly supported dataset signal. It is positive and interval-excluding-zero in batch_a (H111, +0.234, 95% CI +0.125 to +0.342; R109), in the dominant Avana library (H112, +0.288, 95% CI +0.232 to +0.343; R110), and in STK11-loss cells (H113, +0.258, 95% CI +0.134 to +0.382; R111). H113 is scientifically interesting because STK11-loss is a relevant co-mutation context and the PTEN-loss exposed cell count is only 50, but the effect size and lower bound are still meaningful. I accept H111, H112, and H113 as dataset associations, and request independent validation only for H113 because it has the smallest exposed cell among these accepted PTEN/STAT3 contexts and is the most useful remaining robustness check. H114 confirms that KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 is robust in STK11-loss cells (+0.775, 95% CI +0.727 to +0.823; R112). H115 confirms TP53-intact/USP7 in STK11-loss cells (+0.490, 95% CI +0.312 to +0.667; R113). H116 confirms SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 in TP53-loss cells (+0.773, 95% CI +0.729 to +0.817; R114). These effects are enormous relative to the dependency-score scale, interval-excluding-zero, and do not require additional validation. The new mechanism probe H110 shows no meaningful association between KEAP1 loss and STAT3 dependency (+0.016, 95% CI -0.012 to +0.044; R108), so it is rejected. H25, H30, H73, and H77 are all small or interval-crossing and are rejected: KRAS mutation in STK11-intact cells does not show meaningful dependency_KRAS association; MYC amplification does not show dependency_POLR2A association; PIK3CA mutation does not meaningfully modify TP53-intact/USP7; and research marker E does not show WRN association. H98 cannot be assessed because the PTEN-loss by SMAD4-loss comparison has only 19 exposed cases, violating the cell-size rule; it remains unresolved and deferred as underpowered rather than rejected. Independent validation is requested for H113 because it is a newly accepted context-specific PTEN/STAT3 result with the greatest remaining uncertainty, while validation capacity remains limited.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims: (1) MSI-high -> much stronger dependency_WRN: main validated R8/R39; contexts include adenocarcinoma R27, batch_a R28, Avana R41, KY R105. (2) SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger dependency_SMARCA2: main validated R9/R26; ARID1A-intact R75, ARID1A-loss R65/R66, adenocarcinoma R32, batch_a R29, KY R42, TP53-loss R114. (3) TP53-intact -> stronger dependency_USP7: main validated R12/R40; adenocarcinoma R34, batch_a R30, KY R43/R53, STK11-loss R113. (4) KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative dependency_NFE2L2: main validated R7/R13; adenocarcinoma R33, batch_a R31, KY R44, STK11-loss R112. (5) PTEN loss -> stronger dependency_STAT3: main validated R73/R79; adenocarcinoma R81, TP53-intact R84, TP53-loss R85/R93, KEAP1-loss R102, KY R101/R106, batch_a R109, Avana R110, STK11-loss R111 pending validation. Current rejected/null findings: KEAP1 loss is not associated with dependency_STAT3 overall R108. KRAS mutation in STK11-intact cells is not associated with dependency_KRAS R115. MYC amplification is not associated with dependency_POLR2A R116, TMED10 R45, RPL11 R21, DHX9 R64, or KIF18A R78. PIK3CA mutation does not modify TP53-intact/USP7 R117 and does not modify PTEN/STAT3 R83/R107. Research marker E is not associated with dependency_WRN R118. EGFR amplification remains unsupported for dependency_EGFR, TMED10, ERBB2, and STAT3 in tested analyses. PTEN loss remains specific among tested outcomes: no overall USP7 R103 or MDM2 R104 association. H98 PTEN/STAT3 by SMAD4-loss interaction is untestable due insufficient exposed cell count R119 and remains deferred. Main remaining uncertainty: independent validation response for H113 PTEN/STAT3 in STK11-loss cells.",
